    "topic": "isPalindrome()",
    "question": "<p>2. Consider the following structure for a word:</p><pre class=\"sheet\">struct Word{\n       char elements[MAX];\n       int length;\n\n};</pre><p>A word is a palindrome if it is exactly the same as the word itself, when written in the reversed order. For example: “dad” and “mom” are palindromes. “grace” is not a palindrome because the reversed word order gives “ecarg”. Assume the characters are in lower case. Propose an algorithm called isPalindrome() with appropriate input parameter(s) and returned value, which can be used to determine if a word is a palindrome or not. (4 marks)</p>",
    "think": "",
    "solution": "<pre class=\"code\"><span class=\"ln\" style=\"--ind:0\"><span class=\"lead\"></span><span class=\"k\">bool</span> isPalindrome(Word *w) {</span><span class=\"ln\" style=\"--ind:4\"><span class=\"lead\">    </span><span class=\"k\">int</span> left = 0;</span><span class=\"ln\" style=\"--ind:4\"><span class=\"lead\">    </span><span class=\"k\">int</span> right = w-&gt;length - 1;</span><span class=\"ln\" style=\"--ind:4\"><span class=\"lead\">    </span><span class=\"k\">while</span> (left &lt; right) {</span><span class=\"ln\" style=\"--ind:8\"><span class=\"lead\">        </span><span class=\"k\">if</span> (w-&gt;elements[left] != w-&gt;elements[right])</span><span class=\"ln\" style=\"--ind:12\"><span class=\"lead\">            </span><span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"k\">false</span>;<span class=\"c c-trail\"><span class=\"pad\">             </span>// a mismatch: not a palindrome</span></span><span class=\"ln\" style=\"--ind:8\"><span class=\"lead\">        </span>left++;</span><span class=\"ln\" style=\"--ind:8\"><span class=\"lead\">        </span>right--;</span><span class=\"ln\" style=\"--ind:4\"><span class=\"lead\">    </span>}</span><span class=\"ln\" style=\"--ind:4\"><span class=\"lead\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"k\">true</span>;<span class=\"c c-trail\"><span class=\"pad\">                      </span>// every pair matched</span></span><span class=\"ln\" style=\"--ind:0\"><span class=\"lead\"></span>}</span></pre><p>Input: the word (a pointer to <code>Word</code>). Returns <code>true</code> if it is a palindrome, <code>false</code> otherwise. “dad” → true, “grace” → false (g ≠ e).</p>"
